                <pb facs="0957" n="867" sameAs="frus:frus1920v02/pg867"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">815.00/2204: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Honduras</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Belden</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tegucigalpa</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-07-11T17:00:00-05:48"><hi rendition="#italic">July 11, 1920—5
                                p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received July 12—10:47
                    a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>49. Serious rumors from all sections of the country and a very open
                    dissatisfaction with the present administration cause me to apprehend a
                    revolutionary movement shortly. Present Government is weak and has lost its
                    financial credit and many former friends and the general situation is very
                    serious.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Belden</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
